cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Archaic-DNA processing pipeline: a modular archaeogenetics pipeline for detecting unexpected archaic introgression"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kuhn
    given-names: Bennett
repository-code: "https://github.com/bennettek99-spec/Archaic-DNA-processing-pipeline"
license: MIT
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-08-16
keywords:
  - archaeogenetics
  - ancient DNA
  - Neanderthal introgression
  - f-statistics
  - AADR
abstract: >-
  A modular, validated Python pipeline that estimates Neanderthal ancestry and
  relative Denisovan affinity in ancient and present-day genomes from the Allen
  Ancient DNA Resource using allele-frequency f-statistics with block-jackknife
  errors. It separates raw numerical maxima from credibility-aware results and
  is validated against published estimates, coalescent simulations with known
  ground truth, and ADMIXTOOLS 2.
